<tr id="S4.T2.3.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/156_0-prompt_0-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g7" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"> <img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/156_2-prompt_0-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g8" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"> <img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/156_4-prompt_0-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g9" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/429_0-prompt_0-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g10" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"> <img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/429_0-prompt_1-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g11" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"> <img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/429_6-prompt_1-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g12" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.3.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span> <span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.1.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">5. <span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">the view from one end of a bench in a park, looking</span></span></span>
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.1.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.1.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">at the sky with the text ‘imagine the outcome’ in the sky</span></span></span>
</span></span><span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.1.3" class="ltx_text"></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_text"></span> <span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.2.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">6. <span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">the hubble telescope and the milky way, with the text</span></span></span>
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.2.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.2.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">‘the universe is a mystery, but we are here to solve it’</span></span></span>
</span></span><span id="S4.T2.3.1.5.2.3" class="ltx_text"></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.3.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/165_0-prompt_0-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g13" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"> <img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/165_0-prompt_1-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g14" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"> <img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/165_6-prompt_0-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g15" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/163_0-prompt_0-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g16" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"> <img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/163_0-prompt_1-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g17" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"> <img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/163_6-prompt_1-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g18" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.3.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span> <span id="S4.T2.3.1.7.1.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.7.1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.7.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.7.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">7. <span id="S4.T2.3.1.7.1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">a picture of multiple trees at various stages of development,</span></span></span>
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.7.1.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S4.T2.3.1.7.1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.7.1.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">with the caption ‘growth is a continuous process’</span></span></span>
</span></span><span id="S4.T2.3.1.7.1.3" class="ltx_text"></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">8. <span id="S4.T2.3.1.7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">a stained glass window depicting a calm tyrannosaurus rex</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.3.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/102_0-prompt_1-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g19" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"> <img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/102_0-prompt_0-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g20" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"> <img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/102_4-prompt_0-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g21" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/105_0-prompt_0-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g22" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"> <img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/105_2-prompt_1-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g23" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"> <img src="2509.10704v1/figs/qualitative_analysis/105_6-prompt_1-batch_0.png" id="S4.T2.g24" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:143/143;" width="143" height="143" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Qualitative examples of the image trajectories generated by <span id="S4.T2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> using different <span id="S4.T2.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">original</span> user prompts (which are given at the top of each image row). Each row, from left to right, shows 1) image generated using the original, unaltered user prompt; 2) an intermediate generation, and 3) the final, optimized image returned by <span id="S4.T2.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> after to up to 8 iterations. Refer to App. <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Additional Qualitative Results ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> for additional visualizations and the text prompts that generated the presented images.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F7.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10704v1/ablation.svg" id="S4.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/274;" width="476" height="274"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F7.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10704v1/ablation_dsg.svg" id="S4.F7.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/274;" width="476" height="274"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F7.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="S4.F7.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation studies showing <span id="S4.F7.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(left)</span> pairwise AutoSxS advantage distributions (note that first 4 rows are compared w.r.t. the images generated by the original prompt; the final row compares <span id="S4.F7.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> (full algorithm) against P+I+R variant; <span id="S4.F7.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(right)</span> pointwise DSGScore of the different algorithmic variants.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation studies.</span> To understand the contribution of different components of our system, we also conducted ablation studies on a dataset randomly subsampled from p2-hard and DSG-1K and we study the following <span id="S4.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> variants in Fig. <a href="#S4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>:</p>
<ol id="S4.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">R</span>: Prompts generated by the initial <span id="S4.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">R</span>ewriting (§<a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Initialization (Blocks 1-3 in Fig. ) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) only;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">I+R</span>: Prompts generated by initial <span id="S4.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">R</span>ewriting and the <span id="S4.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">I</span>terative improvements (§<a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Initialization (Blocks 1-3 in Fig. ) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> &amp; §<a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Generating New Prompt Proposals (Blocks 7-9) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>) where we always iterate upon the <span id="S4.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">last generation</span> (i.e., without tracking <span id="S4.I3.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the best generation so far</span> discussed in §<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Pairwise Objective and Comparator (Block 6) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> or the self-verification and correction mechanism in §<a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 User Intent Grounding via Self-Verification (Block 10) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S4.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">P+I+R</span>: Same as above, but with <span id="S4.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P</span>airwise comparator (§<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Pairwise Objective and Comparator (Block 6) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>) added to track and improve upon the best generation so far (rather than simply iterating on the last iteration);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S4.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span><span id="S4.I3.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"> (V+P+I+R)</span>: the full <span id="S4.I3.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> algorithm; the difference w.r.t. the previous method is the introduction of the self-<span id="S4.I3.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">V</span>erification component (§<a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 User Intent Grounding via Self-Verification (Block 10) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">By default, we compared each of the variants against the image generated with the original user prompts (<span id="S4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Orig.</span>), although we added one experiment directly comparing <span id="S4.p9.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span><span id="S4.p9.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"> (V+P+I+R)</span> and <span id="S4.p9.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">P+I+R</span> given that they achieved similar advantage against <span id="S4.p9.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Orig.</span> (5.88 vs 5.84); we find that the full <span id="S4.p9.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> still has a modest advantage over <span id="S4.p9.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">P+I+R</span> when compared head-to-head and a bigger improvement in terms of DSGScore–this is unsurprising as the goal of self-verification component is to ground the newly generated prompts to the user intent, which is reflected by the improvement in DSGScore that tracks the prompt-image consistency. On the other hand, the addition of the other components unequivocally improved both AutoSxS score and the DSGScore, demonstrating the utility of each component of <span id="S4.p9.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> in improving the overall performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present <span id="S5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span>, a novel multi-agent system that empowers T2I models to autonomously refine their output through iterative prompt adjustments. By leveraging multi-agent critique with interpretable feedback and a pairwise MLLM-as-a-judge objective for robust evaluation, <span id="S5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> significantly improves image quality over initial prompts and state-of-the-art techniques, with benefits scaling with MLLM advancements. We believe the scope for future work is ample: for example, while our current evaluations focus on the Imagen model, the framework’s model-agnostic design invites future testing across diverse T2I systems which is an immediate next step. Second, while we have focused on T2I generation, the core principles of <span id="S5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> also show promise for general generative tasks lacking ground truths and that might benefit from targeted supervision for editing, including but not limited to, for example, <span id="S5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">audio</span> or <span id="S5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">video</span> synthesis. Lastly, while <span id="S5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> is currently a test-time algorithm, the generated improvement trajectories could be integrated into the T2I model training pipeline, enabling autonomous self-improvement beyond prompt refinement – we leave these important explorations to future work.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\nobibliography</span>
<p id="S5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">*</p>
</div>
</section>
