</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we describe the implementation details, including the prompt templates used in different stages of <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> aside from the ones listed in the main text and the specific hyperparameters used in both <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> and the baselines.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialization (§<a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Initialization (Blocks 1-3 in Fig. ) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>)</span>
We show the prompt template for the initial LLM rewrite below, using the Jinja2 syntax with the brace-enclosed variables to be replaced with actual values during compilation, where <span id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">current_prompt</span> denotes the original, user prompt <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> with <span id="A1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">n_prompt</span> set to 1 by default. The output is extracted by the regex <span id="A1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PROMPT&gt;(.*?)&lt;/PROMPT&gt;</span>. Note that we also use the prompt below for the ‘Rewrite’ baseline.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="591.24" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 676.77 591.24" width="676.77"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,591.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#808040;" fill="#808040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 0 583.37 C 0 587.72 3.53 591.24 7.87 591.24 L 668.9 591.24 C 673.25 591.24 676.77 587.72 676.77 583.37 L 676.77 7.87 C 676.77 3.53 673.25 0 668.9 0 L 7.87 0 C 3.53 0 0 3.53 0 7.87 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFD9;" fill="#FFFFD9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 9.84 L 1.97 565.59 L 674.8 565.59 L 674.8 9.84 C 674.8 5.49 671.28 1.97 666.93 1.97 L 9.84 1.97 C 5.49 1.97 1.97 5.49 1.97 9.84 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 574.96)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.81em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="550.86"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.81em;">
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Prompt template for initial rewrite (§<a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Initialization (Blocks 1-3 in Fig. ) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 15.72)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:57.42em;--ltx-fo-height:38.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="540.01" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 538.07)" width="794.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:57.42em;">
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Hi Gemini, I want to create an image by giving a prompt to Imagen, a text-to-image model.</span></span>
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Here is my current prompt:
"{ <span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">current_prompt</span> }"</span></span>
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Please generate an improved prompt based on the following guidelines for Imagen:</span></span>
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. Make sure the prompt contains the elements of <span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">subject</span>, <span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">context</span>, and <span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">style</span>. Specifically, 
<br class="ltx_break">- Subject: The first thing to think about with any prompt is the subject: the object, person, animal, or scenery you want an image of. 
<br class="ltx_break">- Context and background: Just as important is the background or context in which the subject will be placed. Try placing your subject in a variety of backgrounds. For example, a studio with a white background, outdoors, or indoor environments. 
<br class="ltx_break">- Style: Finally, add the style of image you want. Styles can be general (painting, photograph, sketches) or very specific (pastel painting, charcoal drawing, isometric 3D).</span></span>
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. Use descriptive language: Employ detailed adjectives and adverbs to paint a clear picture for Imagen 3.</span></span>
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. Provide context: If necessary, include background information to aid the AI’s understanding.</span></span>
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4. Reference specific artists or styles: If you have a particular aesthetic in mind, referencing specific artists or art movements can be helpful.</span></span>
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">5. Use prompt engineering tools: Consider exploring prompt engineering tools or resources to help you refine your prompts and achieve optimal results.</span></span>
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">6. Enhancing the facial details in your personal and group images: 
<br class="ltx_break">- Specify facial details as a focus of the photo (for example, use the word "portrait" in the prompt).</span></span>
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Please now generate { <span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">n_prompt</span> } improved prompt(s) and enclose any new prompt between <span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.10.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PROMPT&gt;</span> and <span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.10.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/PROMPT&gt;</span>.
If you believe the current prompt is already satisfactory, simply respond with <span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.10.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"&lt;PROMPT&gt; NO_CHANGE &lt;/PROMPT&gt;"</span>.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For the DVQs, we re-used the instructions and few-shot examples provided by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cho et al. (2024)</a></cite> to decompose a given user prompt to a list of DVQs. These DVQs were generated once, and are subsequently fixed for all methods that use these questions (e.g., <span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> and OPT2I).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pairwise comparison (§<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Pairwise Objective and Comparator (Block 6) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>)</span> While we have already included the prompt for pairwise comparison in §<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Pairwise Objective and Comparator (Block 6) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> in the main text, here we give additional implementation details: as discussed, at the end of each prompt generation step, we perform binary tournament amongst the newly generated prompt-image pairs first (if more than one image is generated in the step): we ask the MLLM to choose a preferred image between a pair of images (denoted as Image A and Image B) for <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n</annotation></semantics></math> times (we set <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3</annotation></semantics></math> by default) in parallel (for the first <math id="A1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> times, the model will place Image A first and for the remaining <math id="A1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> times, the model will place Image B first to eliminate position bias). This process continues until there is a single candidate prompt remaining, which is denoted the <span id="A1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">best prompt so far</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt generation (§<a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Generating New Prompt Proposals (Blocks 7-9) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>)</span>
Below we show the prompt templates given to the LLM to generate new prompt(s) based on previous feedback (§<a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Generating New Prompt Proposals (Blocks 7-9) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>), and we use the following templates for <span id="A1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">targeted editing</span>, which consists of 1) visual question answering by an MLLM, given the DVQs in the previous step and 2) generating new prompts given by the DVQs along with the LLM’s answers. For the first step, by default we break it into two LLM calls: firstly asking the model to give an answer <span id="A1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">without explaining</span>, followed by another call instructing the model to <span id="A1.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">rationalize</span> its answer in a posthoc manner – it is worth noting that a (potentially better) alternative is to simply use chain-of-thought (CoT) style prompting and retain the rationale part, but we opted for posthoc rationalization to ensure fairness of comparison against the baselines (which relies on the final answer given by the LLM only) and to avoid the discrepancy introduced by using the CoT-style template, which may influence the MLLM prediction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p7.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="192.45" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 676.77 192.45" width="676.77"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,192.45) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#8080FF;" fill="#8080FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 0 184.58 C 0 188.93 3.53 192.45 7.87 192.45 L 668.9 192.45 C 673.25 192.45 676.77 188.93 676.77 184.58 L 676.77 7.87 C 676.77 3.53 673.25 0 668.9 0 L 7.87 0 C 3.53 0 0 3.53 0 7.87 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#D9D9FF;" fill="#D9D9FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 9.84 L 1.97 134.36 L 674.8 134.36 L 674.8 9.84 C 674.8 5.49 671.28 1.97 666.93 1.97 L 9.84 1.97 C 5.49 1.97 1.97 5.49 1.97 9.84 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 143.73)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.81em;--ltx-fo-height:3.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="46.28" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 42.82)" width="550.86"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p7.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.81em;">
<span id="A1.p7.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Prompt template for DVQ <span id="A1.p7.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">question-answering</span> (§<a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Generating New Prompt Proposals (Blocks 7-9) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.2)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:57.42em;--ltx-fo-height:7.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="108.78" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 106.35)" width="794.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p7.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:57.42em;">
<span id="A1.p7.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer only with ‘yes’ or ‘no’. Do not give other outputs or punctuation marks. 
<br class="ltx_break">Image: { <span id="A1.p7.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">image</span> } 
<br class="ltx_break">Question: { <span id="A1.p7.pic1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dvq[i]</span> }</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p8.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="242.27" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 676.77 242.27" width="676.77"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,242.27) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#8080FF;" fill="#8080FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 0 234.39 C 0 238.74 3.53 242.27 7.87 242.27 L 668.9 242.27 C 673.25 242.27 676.77 238.74 676.77 234.39 L 676.77 7.87 C 676.77 3.53 673.25 0 668.9 0 L 7.87 0 C 3.53 0 0 3.53 0 7.87 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#D9D9FF;" fill="#D9D9FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 9.84 L 1.97 184.18 L 674.8 184.18 L 674.8 9.84 C 674.8 5.49 671.28 1.97 666.93 1.97 L 9.84 1.97 C 5.49 1.97 1.97 5.49 1.97 9.84 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 193.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.81em;--ltx-fo-height:3.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="46.28" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 42.82)" width="550.86"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p8.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.81em;">
<span id="A1.p8.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Prompt template for DVQ <span id="A1.p8.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">rationalization</span> (§<a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Generating New Prompt Proposals (Blocks 7-9) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.2)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:57.42em;--ltx-fo-height:11.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="158.59" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 156.17)" width="794.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p8.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:57.42em;">
<span id="A1.p8.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are an expert in examining images generated by text-to-image generation models. The user specifies a list of questions, each of which contains a property or characteristic that the generated image should have and the goal is to make sure that when an reviewer reviews the generated image, they will answer “Yes" to each of these questions. However, the reviewer answered “No" to the question below to the current image: 
<br class="ltx_break">Image: { <span id="A1.p8.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">image</span> } 
<br class="ltx_break">Question: { <span id="A1.p8.pic1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dvq[i]</span> }</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">For the actual prompt generation step, we used the following template for the <span id="A1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">targeted editing</span> generator, where <span id="A1.p9.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">best_prompt_so_far</span> is the best prompt so far <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p^{*}_{:t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}_{:t}</annotation></semantics></math> as determined by the Comparator (§<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Pairwise Objective and Comparator (Block 6) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>); <span id="A1.p9.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">n_questions</span> denotes the number of decomposed visual questions (DVQs) (discussed in §<a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Initialization (Blocks 1-3 in Fig. ) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>); <span id="A1.p9.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dvq</span> is a list of actual DVQ, and <span id="A1.p9.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">feedback</span> the MLLM response to the rationalization question above:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p10.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="739.55" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 676.77 739.55" width="676.77"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,739.55) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#00B300;" fill="#00B300" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 0 731.68 C 0 736.03 3.53 739.55 7.87 739.55 L 668.9 739.55 C 673.25 739.55 676.77 736.03 676.77 731.68 L 676.77 7.87 C 676.77 3.53 673.25 0 668.9 0 L 7.87 0 C 3.53 0 0 3.53 0 7.87 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#D9FFD9;" fill="#D9FFD9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 9.84 L 1.97 713.9 L 674.8 713.9 L 674.8 9.84 C 674.8 5.49 671.28 1.97 666.93 1.97 L 9.84 1.97 C 5.49 1.97 1.97 5.49 1.97 9.84 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 723.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.81em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="550.86"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p10.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.81em;">
<span id="A1.p10.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Prompt template for targeted editing (§<a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Generating New Prompt Proposals (Blocks 7-9) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 14.59)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:57.42em;--ltx-fo-height:49.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.06em;font-size:10pt;" height="688.32" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 687.51)" width="794.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p10.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:57.42em;">
<span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are an expert in prompt engineering for text-to-image generation models, which take a text prompt as input and generate images depicting the prompt as output. Your task is to improve upon my current prompt based on feedback I obtained from human reviewers.</span></span>
<span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The user has specified a list of questions, each of which contains a property or characteristic that the generated image should have and the goal is to make sure that when a reviewer reviews the generatd image, they will answer ‘Yes’ to all the questions. However, they have answered ‘No’ to one or more questions and provided some feedback, and I’d like you to help me improve my existing prompt, taking into account their feedback.</span></span>
<span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">My current prompt is:
<br class="ltx_break">‘{ <span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">best_prompt_so_far</span> }’</span></span>
<span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">But a reviewer looked at my image and answered ‘No’ to the following question(s). Below are the questions and their feedback, which contains explanations why they believed the image does not satisfy the requirement in the question(s) and their suggestions for improvements:</span></span>
<span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{% <span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">for i in range(n_questions)</span> %} 
<br class="ltx_break">Question {<span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"> i + 1 </span>}: 
<br class="ltx_break">{ <span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dvq[i]</span> } 
<br class="ltx_break">Feedback { <span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.5.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">i + 1</span> }: 
<br class="ltx_break">{ <span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.5.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">feedback[i]</span> } 
<br class="ltx_break">{ <span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.5.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">end_for</span> } 
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Based on your analysis and the reviewer’s opinion, now improve my prompt by incorporating all their feedback points into  <span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">new_solutions</span>  new prompt(s) so that the reviewer will now answer ‘Yes’ to the question(s) when I generate a new image with the new prompt(s). Pay close attention to any points that they mentioned are lacking in the current image, and ensure you incorporate all these information in your revised prompts. Make sure the revised prompts are concise and effective. You may be creative in composing the new prompts, adding new elements, emphasize existing elements, or shuffle the order of the sentences to <span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">emphasize the previously missing characteristics at the beginning of the prompt</span>.
Finally, make sure each prompt you generated is bracketed between <span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PROMPT&gt;</span> and <span id="A1.p10.pic1.2.6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/PROMPT&gt;</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">implicit improvement</span> generator, we use an adapted version of the prompt from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2024)</a></cite> where we 1) make sure it is always iterated on the <span id="A1.p11.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">best image so far</span> (as opposed to the <span id="A1.p11.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">last generation</span>) and 2) we added an option for the model to early terminate with <span id="A1.p11.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PROMPT&gt; NO_CHANGE &lt;/PROMPT&gt;</span> if it decides that the current generation is already satisfactory (the second change is also applied to our implementation of the LM-BBO baseline, since we believe it leads to a better performance than asking the model to keep editing without any termination criterion).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p12.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="374.79" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 676.77 374.79" width="676.77"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,374.79) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B35900;" fill="#B35900" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 0 366.92 C 0 371.27 3.53 374.79 7.87 374.79 L 668.9 374.79 C 673.25 374.79 676.77 371.27 676.77 366.92 L 676.77 7.87 C 676.77 3.53 673.25 0 668.9 0 L 7.87 0 C 3.53 0 0 3.53 0 7.87 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFECD9;" fill="#FFECD9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 9.84 L 1.97 349.15 L 674.8 349.15 L 674.8 9.84 C 674.8 5.49 671.28 1.97 666.93 1.97 L 9.84 1.97 C 5.49 1.97 1.97 5.49 1.97 9.84 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 358.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.81em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="550.86"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p12.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.81em;">
<span id="A1.p12.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Prompt template for implicit improvement (§<a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Generating New Prompt Proposals (Blocks 7-9) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 14.59)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:57.42em;--ltx-fo-height:23.33em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.06em;font-size:10pt;" height="323.56" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 322.75)" width="794.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p12.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:57.42em;">
<span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Hi Gemini, I want to create an image featuring the topic of ‘{ <span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">user_prompt</span> }’</span></span>
<span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Here is my current prompt: 
<br class="ltx_break">‘{ <span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">best_prompt_so_far</span> }’</span></span>
<span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">I asked Imagen to generate an image using the above prompt. Does it correctly reflect the topic?</span></span>
<span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Image: 
<br class="ltx_break">{ <span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">best_image_so_far</span> }</span></span>
<span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If yes, please simply respond with "<span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PROMPT&gt; NO_CHANGE &lt;/PROMPT&gt;</span>".
If no, please help me modify the prompt by generating { <span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">n_prompts</span> } new prompt(s) and respond with any new prompt in between <span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PROMPT&gt;</span> and <span id="A1.p12.pic1.2.5.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/PROMPT&gt;</span>.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">For all experiments using <span id="A1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span>, we always set <span id="A1.p13.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">n_prompts</span> to 1 for both templates and at each generation we invoke both targeted editing and implicit improvement once in parallel – this thus gives two proposed prompts per each iteration. We set the maximum number of T2I calls to be 8 (which translates to 4 total steps per query). For the LM-BBO baseline, we only use the implicit improvement template <span id="A1.p13.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">upon the last generation</span> with <span id="A1.p13.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">n_prompts</span> set to 1 until the maximum T2I model call (8) is reached or the early termination is triggered (i.e., model generating <span id="A1.p13.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PROMPT&gt; NO_CHANGE &lt;/PROMPT&gt;</span>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Human preference studies.</span> For human preference study, we collected responses from 3 human respondents (who are all authors’ colleagues) where we show the human respondents the initial, user prompt and a pair of images (but not the optimized prompts) generated from LM-BBO (the next best method from the automated side-by-side studies) and <span id="A1.p14.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> in an interative Google Colab; the ordering of the images is randomized per pair to ensure that the respondents are unable to guess the method that generated the images. We provided the following instructions to the respondents:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p15.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="408.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 676.77 408.23" width="676.77"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,408.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FF4D4D;" fill="#FF4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 0 400.36 C 0 404.71 3.53 408.23 7.87 408.23 L 668.9 408.23 C 673.25 408.23 676.77 404.71 676.77 400.36 L 676.77 7.87 C 676.77 3.53 673.25 0 668.9 0 L 7.87 0 C 3.53 0 0 3.53 0 7.87 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFD9D9;" fill="#FFD9D9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 9.84 L 1.97 384.12 L 674.8 384.12 L 674.8 9.84 C 674.8 5.49 671.28 1.97 666.93 1.97 L 9.84 1.97 C 5.49 1.97 1.97 5.49 1.97 9.84 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 392.72)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.81em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="550.86"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p15.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.81em;">
<span id="A1.p15.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Instructions for human preference study</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 32.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:53.86em;--ltx-fo-height:24.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:1.36em;font-size:10pt;" height="358.54" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 339.78)" width="745.27"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p15.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:53.86em;">
<span id="A1.p15.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You will be shown <span id="A1.p15.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">a pair of images</span> (i.e., Left Image and Right Image) and an user prompt (in most cases, the prompt you see is an actual user prompt that was entered into a T2I system (e.g., Midjourney or Imagen)).

<br class="ltx_break">Please click "Left Image" or "Right Image" as your preferred image <span id="A1.p15.pic1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">given the user prompt</span> – the ordering ("Left" or "Right") is randomized between <span id="A1.p15.pic1.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">REFERENCE_DIR</span> and <span id="A1.p15.pic1.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CANDIDATE_DIR</span> that you selected above.

<br class="ltx_break">Try to complete as many selections as possible, but you can stop at any time as your response will be immediately stored.

<br class="ltx_break">Some prompts specify command line arguments such as aspect ratio or resolution – please ignore these options when judging the images the model used to generate the provided images do not account for these options.

<br class="ltx_break">In some cases, the user prompt may contain niche / domain information (e.g., specification of artistic styles or they’d like the image to imitate generations from certain engines). In these cases, please take your time and do research if needed, as your previous response was already saved.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.p15.pic1.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Please always select an image even if there is no clear winner between the two options</span> – we deliberately did not provide a tie option. You may consider factors such as overall coherence, high-level aesthetic, and how close the generate images follow the original user prompt to choose a better image. <span id="A1.p15.pic1.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">If the two images are still similar even after considering the above or, in some cases, the two provided images are identical, please simply pick an image randomly</span>.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">where <span id="A1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">REFERENCE_DIR</span> and <span id="A1.p16.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CANDIDATE_DIR</span> by default point to the directory saving the images generated from LM-BBO and <span id="A1.p16.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span>, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Experiments</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Different Judge Models</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we explore the use of different <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">judge</span> models and their influence on the final results and we show the results in Fig. <a href="#A2.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ B.1 Different Judge Models ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> where we use Gemini 1.5 Pro, Gemini 1.5 Flash and Gemini 2.0 Flash as pairwise judge in the AutoSxS studies. Overall, we find that the relative strength of the methods as implied by the side-by-side comparison is consistent, although Gemini 1.5 Flash noticeably generates a larger fraction of “tie” ratings, likely due to its weaker multimodal understanding capabilities and stronger positional bias (e.g., a tie will be returned if a judge model always prefers the first image or second image) compared to the other judge models.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A2.F8.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10704v1/proto-judge-1.5flash.svg" id="A2.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/287;" width="476" height="287"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A2.F8.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10704v1/proto-judge-1.5pro.svg" id="A2.F8.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/287;" width="476" height="287"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A2.F8.fig3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10704v1/proto-judge-2.0flash.svg" id="A2.F8.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/287;" width="476" height="287"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A2.F8.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">AutoSxS win-tie-lose breakdown using different <span id="A2.F8.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">judge</span> models on a dataset subsampled from p2-hard and DSG-1K.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Different Optimizer Models</h3>

<figure id="A2.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10704v1/different_optim_dsg.svg" id="A2.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/112;" width="238" height="112"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A2.F9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">AutoSxS win-tie-lose breakdown using different <span id="A2.F9.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">optimizer</span> models (methods using Gemini 2.0 and 1.5 are marked with 2.0 and 1.5, respectively) on DSG-1K.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also explore using different <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">optimizer</span> model to understand how the models with different multimodal understanding caliber would affect the overall effectiveness of the <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> pipeline. In Fig. <a href="#A2.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ B.2 Different Optimizer Models ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> we show the results of <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> (and baselines) using Gemini 2.0 Flash optimizer model as opposed to Gemini 1.5 optimizer used by default in the main text. Overall, we find that <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> improves with better foundation model as the optimizer model, with the win rate improving both over the baseline methods using the corresponding optimizer model and <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maestro</span> with a weaker model (the last row of Fig. <a href="#A2.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ B.2 Different Optimizer Models ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Additional Qualitative Results</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present additional qualitative results (Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ B.3 Additional Qualitative Results ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) to complement Table  <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> in the main text. We also show the optimized text prompts that led to the generated images in Tables <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ B.3 Additional Qualitative Results ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Maestro: Self-Improving Text-to-Image Generation via Agent Orchestration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> in Table <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T3" class="ltx_table">
